The hardening of Godot's release templates for running untrusted wallpapers. Applied by scripts/prepare.sh to every
slice; README.md lists each hunk, its purpose and why no build option can replace it. Every hunk is
#ifndef TOOLS_ENABLED: the editor that exports packs is stock. Four concerns, nothing else:

1. The deny-list hook (core/object/class_db.{h,cpp}): a ClassName::method named in native-deny-list.json is never
   registered, on every bind path; and the build profile's disabled_classes holds for register_custom_instance_class.
2. Path confinement (core/io/file_access.{h,cpp}, dir_access.cpp, file_access_pack.cpp, main/main.cpp): from
   Main::setup2 on, every path a FileAccess or DirAccess resolves must lie in user:// or the project directory.
3. No bytes decode into an object once a pack can run (core/io/marshalls.cpp).
4. The extension list is read past the pack (core/extension/gdextension_manager.cpp).

